cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it as below (DOI 10.5281/zenodo.24210391). Research preview (v0.1); not peer-reviewed."
type: dataset
title: "TerraUY Evidence Grounding Benchmark (TEGB): Trustworthy Reasoning over Earth Observation Evidence"
version: "0.1"
date-released: "2026-11-13"
authors:
  - family-names: "Rifrán"
    given-names: "Jairo"
    affiliation: "TerraUY Intelligence"
license:
  - Apache-2.0
  - CC-BY-4.0
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24210391"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.24210391"
    description: "TEGB v0.1 (Zenodo)"
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.24210390"
    description: "All versions (Zenodo concept DOI)"
repository-code: "https://github.com/terrauy/terrauy-evidence-grounding"
url: "https://github.com/terrauy/terrauy-evidence-grounding"
abstract: >-
  A benchmark for evaluating whether AI agents respect what Earth Observation evidence supports and what it does not
  establish. v0.1 (research preview): 82 tasks (74 in 10 failure families plus 8 controls), three evidence
  presentations (RAW, TEXT, STRUCTURED), and an initial baseline of four models (2,952 responses) scored by two blind
  LLM judges and a deterministic detector. Code is Apache-2.0; TEGB-authored tasks, annotations, documentation and
  figures are CC BY 4.0; model outputs are under MODEL_OUTPUTS_NOTICE.md; third-party EO values keep their original terms.
  Not independently reviewed by Earth Observation experts.
keywords:
  - Earth observation
  - remote sensing
  - evidence grounding
  - LLM agents
  - benchmark
  - unsupported conclusions
  - trustworthy AI
